  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "how_to_play",
      "markdown": "An early form of chess from India, with its own pieces:\n\n- **Raja** (king): one step in any direction, never onto an attacked square.\n- **Mantri** (counsellor): one step diagonally.\n- **Gaja** (elephant): jumps exactly two squares diagonally.\n- **Ashva** (horse): moves like the chess knight.\n- **Ratha** (chariot): slides in straight lines.\n- **Padati** (foot soldier): steps forward, captures diagonally, and becomes a mantri on the far row.\n\nYou win by checkmate, by leaving your opponent with only a raja, or because your opponent has no move."
    },
